177,Electronics,Basics of Electricity & Electronics,AC Circuit Analysis: Reactance & Impedance — Why AC needs more than resistance [e703c370],"Capacitors and inductors oppose AC current in a way that depends on frequency, and -- unlike a resistor -- they also shift the timing (phase) between voltage and current. Reactance is the AC equivalent of resistance for these frequency-dependent components, measured in ohms.",electricity-electronics-basics;ac-circuit-analysis-impedance;lesson_passage,https://munsakad.github.io/Hardware-Engineering-Education-Hub/pages/course.html?slug=electricity-electronics-basics&lesson=ac-circuit-analysis-impedance,lesson:electricity-electronics-basics/ac-circuit-analysis-impedance,lesson_passage
