229,Digital Logic Design,Digital Logic Design,Binary Arithmetic & Signed Numbers — Representing negative numbers: complements [e6a06b13],"Digital systems have no separate minus-sign wire, so negative numbers are encoded using complements.",digital-logic-design;binary-arithmetic-signed-numbers;lesson_passage,https://munsakad.github.io/Hardware-Engineering-Education-Hub/pages/course.html?slug=digital-logic-design&lesson=binary-arithmetic-signed-numbers,lesson:digital-logic-design/binary-arithmetic-signed-numbers,lesson_passage
230,Digital Logic Design,Digital Logic Design,Binary Arithmetic & Signed Numbers — Representing negative numbers: complements [2b662e88],"Complement systems for an n-bit number N | System | Rule | Example (4-bit, N = 0110) | 1′s complement | Flip every bit | 0110 → 1001 | 2′s complement | Flip every bit, then add 1 | 0110 → 1001 + 1 = 1010",digital-logic-design;binary-arithmetic-signed-numbers;lesson_passage,https://munsakad.github.io/Hardware-Engineering-Education-Hub/pages/course.html?slug=digital-logic-design&lesson=binary-arithmetic-signed-numbers,lesson:digital-logic-design/binary-arithmetic-signed-numbers,lesson_passage
231,Digital Logic Design,Digital Logic Design,Binary Arithmetic & Signed Numbers — Representing negative numbers: complements [f6b2fd81],"Two′s complement is what almost all real hardware uses, because it has a single representation for zero and turns subtraction into addition.",digital-logic-design;binary-arithmetic-signed-numbers;lesson_passage,https://munsakad.github.io/Hardware-Engineering-Education-Hub/pages/course.html?slug=digital-logic-design&lesson=binary-arithmetic-signed-numbers,lesson:digital-logic-design/binary-arithmetic-signed-numbers,lesson_passage
232,Digital Logic Design,Digital Logic Design,Binary Arithmetic & Signed Numbers — Two′s complement representation [4e88f5cd],"In an n-bit two′s complement number, the most significant bit (MSB) is a sign bit: 0 means positive, 1 means negative. To negate a number, take its two′s complement.",digital-logic-design;binary-arithmetic-signed-numbers;lesson_passage,https://munsakad.github.io/Hardware-Engineering-Education-Hub/pages/course.html?slug=digital-logic-design&lesson=binary-arithmetic-signed-numbers,lesson:digital-logic-design/binary-arithmetic-signed-numbers,lesson_passage
