246,Digital Logic Design,Digital Logic Design,Boolean Algebra Basics — Three equivalent descriptions of the same logic [8f3f0e21],"A literal is a single variable or its complement (e.g. A or A′). A product term (like A′B) is a set of literals ANDed together, and a sum-of-products expression is several product terms ORed together.",digital-logic-design;boolean-algebra-basics;lesson_passage,https://munsakad.github.io/Hardware-Engineering-Education-Hub/pages/course.html?slug=digital-logic-design&lesson=boolean-algebra-basics,lesson:digital-logic-design/boolean-algebra-basics,lesson_passage
