250,Digital Logic Design,Digital Logic Design,Laws of Boolean Algebra — Commutative and associative laws [4ed5f9be],Commutative and associative laws | Law | AND form | OR form | Commutative | AB = BA | A + B = B + A | Associative | (AB)C = A(BC) | (A + B) + C = A + (B + C),digital-logic-design;laws-of-boolean-algebra;lesson_passage,https://munsakad.github.io/Hardware-Engineering-Education-Hub/pages/course.html?slug=digital-logic-design&lesson=laws-of-boolean-algebra,lesson:digital-logic-design/laws-of-boolean-algebra,lesson_passage
251,Digital Logic Design,Digital Logic Design,Laws of Boolean Algebra — Distributive and absorption laws [06b699d6],Distributive and absorption laws | Law | Statement | Distributive | A(B + C) = AB + AC | Distributive (dual) | A + BC = (A + B)(A + C) | Absorption | A + AB = A | Absorption (variant) | A(A + B) = A | Absorption (variant 2) | A + A′B = A + B,digital-logic-design;laws-of-boolean-algebra;lesson_passage,https://munsakad.github.io/Hardware-Engineering-Education-Hub/pages/course.html?slug=digital-logic-design&lesson=laws-of-boolean-algebra,lesson:digital-logic-design/laws-of-boolean-algebra,lesson_passage
252,Digital Logic Design,Digital Logic Design,Laws of Boolean Algebra — Distributive and absorption laws [df34c559],Absorption is one of the most useful simplification tools -- it lets you eliminate a redundant term that is already covered by a simpler one.,digital-logic-design;laws-of-boolean-algebra;lesson_passage,https://munsakad.github.io/Hardware-Engineering-Education-Hub/pages/course.html?slug=digital-logic-design&lesson=laws-of-boolean-algebra,lesson:digital-logic-design/laws-of-boolean-algebra,lesson_passage
253,Digital Logic Design,Digital Logic Design,Laws of Boolean Algebra — Consensus (redundancy) theorem [05dc9d05],"The term BC is the ""consensus"" of AB and A′C (formed by combining the non-complementary variables of two terms that contain a variable and its complement). It is always redundant algebraically and can be dropped -- though, as the timing lesson later in this course shows, that exact redundant term is sometimes deliberately kept in real hardware to prevent a glitch.",digital-logic-design;laws-of-boolean-algebra;lesson_passage,https://munsakad.github.io/Hardware-Engineering-Education-Hub/pages/course.html?slug=digital-logic-design&lesson=laws-of-boolean-algebra,lesson:digital-logic-design/laws-of-boolean-algebra,lesson_passage
254,Digital Logic Design,Digital Logic Design,Laws of Boolean Algebra — De Morgan′s theorems [f7ece541],De Morgan′s theorems | Form | Statement | In words | 1 | (A + B)′ = A′ · B′ | NOT of an OR = AND of the NOTs | 2 | (A · B)′ = A′ + B′ | NOT of an AND = OR of the NOTs,digital-logic-design;laws-of-boolean-algebra;lesson_passage,https://munsakad.github.io/Hardware-Engineering-Education-Hub/pages/course.html?slug=digital-logic-design&lesson=laws-of-boolean-algebra,lesson:digital-logic-design/laws-of-boolean-algebra,lesson_passage
