256,Digital Logic Design,Digital Logic Design,Laws of Boolean Algebra — The principle of duality [f275e5cb],"Every Boolean identity has a ""dual,"" formed by swapping AND ↔ OR and 0 ↔ 1 everywhere. For example, the dual of A + A′B = A + B is A(A′ + B) = AB. This is why the laws above are almost always listed in AND/OR pairs.",digital-logic-design;laws-of-boolean-algebra;lesson_passage,https://munsakad.github.io/Hardware-Engineering-Education-Hub/pages/course.html?slug=digital-logic-design&lesson=laws-of-boolean-algebra,lesson:digital-logic-design/laws-of-boolean-algebra,lesson_passage
