294,Digital Logic Design,Digital Logic Design,Karnaugh Maps & Minimization — Do not care conditions [a0eef99f],"Some input combinations may never actually occur (e.g. BCD digit codes 1010-1111), or their output may not matter for a given application. These are marked ""X"" (don′t care) on the map. You are free to treat each X as a 0 or a 1, whichever helps form a larger group -- but you are never required to cover an X.",digital-logic-design;karnaugh-maps;lesson_passage,https://munsakad.github.io/Hardware-Engineering-Education-Hub/pages/course.html?slug=digital-logic-design&lesson=karnaugh-maps,lesson:digital-logic-design/karnaugh-maps,lesson_passage
