296,Digital Logic Design,Digital Logic Design,"Combinational Circuit Design — What makes a circuit ""combinational"" [335e7345]","A combinational circuit′s outputs depend only on its current inputs, with no memory of the past. Every circuit covered in the next several lessons -- adders, multiplexers, decoders, comparators -- is combinational; sequential circuits (with memory) are covered later in this course.",digital-logic-design;combinational-circuit-design;lesson_passage,https://munsakad.github.io/Hardware-Engineering-Education-Hub/pages/course.html?slug=digital-logic-design&lesson=combinational-circuit-design,lesson:digital-logic-design/combinational-circuit-design,lesson_passage
