310,Digital Logic Design,Digital Logic Design,Adders & Subtractors — Ripple-carry adder [2a88ba6c],"Chaining n full adders, with each stage′s Cout feeding the next stage′s Cin, builds an n-bit adder. It is called ""ripple carry"" because a carry generated at the least significant bit may have to propagate (""ripple"") all the way to the most significant bit, making the worst-case delay grow with the number of bits -- the main drawback of this simple design.",digital-logic-design;adders-and-subtractors;lesson_passage,https://munsakad.github.io/Hardware-Engineering-Education-Hub/pages/course.html?slug=digital-logic-design&lesson=adders-and-subtractors,lesson:digital-logic-design/adders-and-subtractors,lesson_passage
