359,Digital Logic Design,Digital Logic Design,Latches & Flip-Flops — Characteristic equations [e5b74fc3],"Characteristic equations | Flip-flop | Characteristic equation | SR | Q(next) = S + R′Q, with the restriction S · R = 0 | D | Q(next) = D | JK | Q(next) = JQ′ + K′Q | T | Q(next) = T ⊕ Q",digital-logic-design;flip-flops-sequential-logic;lesson_passage,https://munsakad.github.io/Hardware-Engineering-Education-Hub/pages/course.html?slug=digital-logic-design&lesson=flip-flops-sequential-logic,lesson:digital-logic-design/flip-flops-sequential-logic,lesson_passage
360,Digital Logic Design,Digital Logic Design,Latches & Flip-Flops — Excitation tables [c71c5ab6],"When designing a sequential circuit, the current state Q and the required next state Q(next) are usually known, and the task is to work out what inputs will produce that transition -- the reverse direction from a characteristic table. An excitation table lists exactly that.",digital-logic-design;flip-flops-sequential-logic;lesson_passage,https://munsakad.github.io/Hardware-Engineering-Education-Hub/pages/course.html?slug=digital-logic-design&lesson=flip-flops-sequential-logic,lesson:digital-logic-design/flip-flops-sequential-logic,lesson_passage
