364,Digital Logic Design,Digital Logic Design,Latches & Flip-Flops — Asynchronous preset and clear [238b93c9],"Most real flip-flop chips add two extra control inputs, Preset (or Set) and Clear (or Reset), which force Q to 1 or 0 immediately, independent of the clock -- used to force a circuit into a known starting state on power-up.",digital-logic-design;flip-flops-sequential-logic;lesson_passage,https://munsakad.github.io/Hardware-Engineering-Education-Hub/pages/course.html?slug=digital-logic-design&lesson=flip-flops-sequential-logic,lesson:digital-logic-design/flip-flops-sequential-logic,lesson_passage
365,Digital Logic Design,Digital Logic Design,Latches & Flip-Flops — Timing parameters [4501eb7f],Key flip-flop timing parameters | Parameter | Meaning | Setup time (t_su) | How long the input must be stable before the clock edge for it to be reliably captured | Hold time (t_h) | How long the input must remain stable after the clock edge | Propagation delay (t_pd / clock-to-Q) | How long after the clock edge it takes for Q to reflect the new value,digital-logic-design;flip-flops-sequential-logic;lesson_passage,https://munsakad.github.io/Hardware-Engineering-Education-Hub/pages/course.html?slug=digital-logic-design&lesson=flip-flops-sequential-logic,lesson:digital-logic-design/flip-flops-sequential-logic,lesson_passage
366,Digital Logic Design,Digital Logic Design,Latches & Flip-Flops — Timing parameters [c16db6c4],"Violating setup or hold time can cause metastability -- the flip-flop output hovers between 0 and 1 for an unpredictable time before settling -- which is why real designs always leave timing margin, verified by static timing analysis, between when data arrives and when the next clock edge samples it.",digital-logic-design;flip-flops-sequential-logic;lesson_passage,https://munsakad.github.io/Hardware-Engineering-Education-Hub/pages/course.html?slug=digital-logic-design&lesson=flip-flops-sequential-logic,lesson:digital-logic-design/flip-flops-sequential-logic,lesson_passage
367,Digital Logic Design,Digital Logic Design,Registers & Shift Registers — Registers [9d9ca640],"A register is simply a group of flip-flops (commonly D flip-flops) sharing a common clock, used to store a multi-bit binary word. A basic parallel-load register loads all its bits simultaneously from a parallel data bus on one clock edge and holds that value until the next load.",digital-logic-design;registers-and-shift-registers;lesson_passage,https://munsakad.github.io/Hardware-Engineering-Education-Hub/pages/course.html?slug=digital-logic-design&lesson=registers-and-shift-registers,lesson:digital-logic-design/registers-and-shift-registers,lesson_passage
368,Digital Logic Design,Digital Logic Design,Registers & Shift Registers — Shift registers [a193982c],"A shift register is a chain of flip-flops where each stage′s output feeds the next stage′s input, so that on every clock edge the stored bits all shift one position, and a new bit enters at one end. Shift registers are classified by how data enters and leaves:",digital-logic-design;registers-and-shift-registers;lesson_passage,https://munsakad.github.io/Hardware-Engineering-Education-Hub/pages/course.html?slug=digital-logic-design&lesson=registers-and-shift-registers,lesson:digital-logic-design/registers-and-shift-registers,lesson_passage
369,Digital Logic Design,Digital Logic Design,Registers & Shift Registers — Shift registers [afec8633],"Shift register types | Type | Data in | Data out | Typical use | SISO (Serial-In, Serial-Out) | Serial | Serial | Fixed-length delay line | SIPO (Serial-In, Parallel-Out) | Serial | Parallel (all bits at once) | Serial-to-parallel conversion (e.g. receiving UART data) | PISO (Parallel-In, Serial-Out) | Parallel (loaded at once) | Serial | Parallel-to-serial conversion (e.g. transmitting UART data) | PIPO (Parallel-In, Parallel-Out) | Parallel | Parallel | Behaves as a simple buffer register",digital-logic-design;registers-and-shift-registers;lesson_passage,https://munsakad.github.io/Hardware-Engineering-Education-Hub/pages/course.html?slug=digital-logic-design&lesson=registers-and-shift-registers,lesson:digital-logic-design/registers-and-shift-registers,lesson_passage
370,Digital Logic Design,Digital Logic Design,Registers & Shift Registers — Universal shift register [238baa60],"A universal shift register combines all these modes into one chip, using a mode-select input to choose the operation performed on each clock edge.",digital-logic-design;registers-and-shift-registers;lesson_passage,https://munsakad.github.io/Hardware-Engineering-Education-Hub/pages/course.html?slug=digital-logic-design&lesson=registers-and-shift-registers,lesson:digital-logic-design/registers-and-shift-registers,lesson_passage
371,Digital Logic Design,Digital Logic Design,Registers & Shift Registers — Universal shift register [f47f4c88],"Universal shift register mode control (typical 2-bit mode select) | S1 | S0 | Operation | 0 | 0 | Hold (no change) | 0 | 1 | Shift right, new bit enters from the left | 1 | 0 | Shift left, new bit enters from the right | 1 | 1 | Parallel load",digital-logic-design;registers-and-shift-registers;lesson_passage,https://munsakad.github.io/Hardware-Engineering-Education-Hub/pages/course.html?slug=digital-logic-design&lesson=registers-and-shift-registers,lesson:digital-logic-design/registers-and-shift-registers,lesson_passage
372,Digital Logic Design,Digital Logic Design,Registers & Shift Registers — Ring counter [dc13d18a],"A ring counter is a shift register whose serial output is fed straight back into its serial input, so a single 1 (or a short pattern) circulates endlessly. An n-bit ring counter cycles through n unique states.",digital-logic-design;registers-and-shift-registers;lesson_passage,https://munsakad.github.io/Hardware-Engineering-Education-Hub/pages/course.html?slug=digital-logic-design&lesson=registers-and-shift-registers,lesson:digital-logic-design/registers-and-shift-registers,lesson_passage
