572,Robotics,Robotics,Ultrasonic & IR Distance Sensing — Choosing between them [017ff5d0],"Ultrasonic vs. IR distance sensing | Aspect | Ultrasonic | IR | Works on dark/black surfaces | Yes -- unaffected by color | Can struggle -- dark surfaces absorb IR light | Works on soft/foam surfaces | Can struggle -- sound absorbed rather than reflected | Generally fine | Affected by ambient light (sunlight) | No | Can be, especially cheaper sensors | Typical response speed | Slower (limited by the speed of sound) | Faster",robotics;ultrasonic-and-ir-distance-sensing;lesson_passage,https://munsakad.github.io/Hardware-Engineering-Education-Hub/pages/course.html?slug=robotics&lesson=ultrasonic-and-ir-distance-sensing,lesson:robotics/ultrasonic-and-ir-distance-sensing,lesson_passage
573,Robotics,Robotics,IMU & Orientation Sensing — Accelerometers and gyroscopes [02a91f3e],"Accelerometer vs. gyroscope | Sensor | Measures | Good at | Weak point | Accelerometer | Linear acceleration (including gravity) on each axis | Long-term tilt reference (gravity always points down) | Noisy, and confused by vibration/motion acceleration mixing with gravity | Gyroscope | Angular velocity (rotation rate) on each axis | Fast, smooth short-term rotation tracking | Drifts over time when integrated into an angle, since small errors accumulate",robotics;imu-and-orientation-sensing;lesson_passage,https://munsakad.github.io/Hardware-Engineering-Education-Hub/pages/course.html?slug=robotics&lesson=imu-and-orientation-sensing,lesson:robotics/imu-and-orientation-sensing,lesson_passage
