578,Robotics,Robotics,IMU & Orientation Sensing — Complementary filter: combining accelerometer and gyroscope [da931b68],"A complementary filter blends the gyroscope′s smooth but drifting short-term estimate with the accelerometer′s noisy but drift-free long-term reference, weighting mostly toward the gyroscope (here, 98%) but slowly correcting toward the accelerometer′s reading over time. More sophisticated robots use a Kalman filter instead, which does the same job with a statistically optimal weighting that adapts based on each sensor′s known noise characteristics, at the cost of considerably more math.",robotics;imu-and-orientation-sensing;lesson_passage,https://munsakad.github.io/Hardware-Engineering-Education-Hub/pages/course.html?slug=robotics&lesson=imu-and-orientation-sensing,lesson:robotics/imu-and-orientation-sensing,lesson_passage
