581,Robotics,Robotics,Line-Following Robots — Computing a line position error [8e198022],"Rather than treating each sensor independently, a weighted average turns the whole sensor array into a single number describing how far off-center the line is:",robotics;line-following-robots;lesson_passage,https://munsakad.github.io/Hardware-Engineering-Education-Hub/pages/course.html?slug=robotics&lesson=line-following-robots,lesson:robotics/line-following-robots,lesson_passage
582,Robotics,Robotics,Line-Following Robots — Computing a line position error [2ef38c4d],"float getLineError() {
    long weightedSum = 0;
    long total = 0;
    const int weights[NUM_SENSORS] = {-2, -1, 0, 1, 2};

    for (int i = 0; i < NUM_SENSORS; i++) {
        weightedSum += (long)sensorValues[i] * weights[i];
        total += sensorValues[i];
    }

    if (total == 0) return 0;   // no line detected by any sensor
    return (float)weightedSum / total;
}",robotics;line-following-robots;code,https://munsakad.github.io/Hardware-Engineering-Education-Hub/pages/course.html?slug=robotics&lesson=line-following-robots,lesson:robotics/line-following-robots,code
