641,Robotics,Robotics,"Safety, Testing & Debugging — Debugging with telemetry [194e3009]","Printing a single, consistent line of key variables like this (rather than scattered individual print statements) makes a running robot′s internal state easy to follow in the Serial Monitor, and easy to log for later analysis if timestamped.",robotics;safety-testing-and-debugging-robots;lesson_passage,https://munsakad.github.io/Hardware-Engineering-Education-Hub/pages/course.html?slug=robotics&lesson=safety-testing-and-debugging-robots,lesson:robotics/safety-testing-and-debugging-robots,lesson_passage
642,Robotics,Robotics,"Safety, Testing & Debugging — Common robot-specific bugs [f3b6bd6d]","Frequent robotics bugs beyond the general Arduino pitfalls | Symptom | Likely cause | Robot drives in a curve instead of straight, with equal commanded speeds | Motors are not actually matched -- mechanical friction and manufacturing variance differ between the two sides; needs a per-motor calibration offset or closed-loop speed control via encoders | Robot resets or behaves erratically only when motors start moving | Motor current surge browning out a shared power supply -- needs separate logic and motor power, as covered in the Robot Power Systems lesson | Distance sensor occasionally reports wildly wrong readings | Reflections off angled surfaces, or crosstalk between multiple ultrasonic sensors firing near-simultaneously | Robot behavior differs noticeably between the bench and the real floor | Real floors have friction, slope, and traction differences a bench test does not reproduce -- always validate on the actual operating surface",robotics;safety-testing-and-debugging-robots;lesson_passage,https://munsakad.github.io/Hardware-Engineering-Education-Hub/pages/course.html?slug=robotics&lesson=safety-testing-and-debugging-robots,lesson:robotics/safety-testing-and-debugging-robots,lesson_passage
643,Digital Logic Design,Verilog,Verilog Syntax Basics — Modules [f765cb08],"Every piece of hardware in Verilog is described inside a module, with a list of input/output ports.",verilog;verilog-syntax-basics;lesson_passage,https://munsakad.github.io/Hardware-Engineering-Education-Hub/pages/course.html?slug=verilog&lesson=verilog-syntax-basics,lesson:verilog/verilog-syntax-basics,lesson_passage
