data  <= std_logic_vector(value);       -- unsigned -> std_logic_vector",vhdl;vhdl-data-types;code,https://munsakad.github.io/Hardware-Engineering-Education-Hub/pages/course.html?slug=vhdl&lesson=vhdl-data-types,lesson:vhdl/vhdl-data-types,code
740,Digital Logic Design,VHDL,VHDL Data Types — integer and other scalar types [5090053e],"integer is useful for things like loop counters and array indices, but is not synthesizable as an arbitrary-width hardware bus the way std_logic_vector is -- it is a simulation and control-flow type, not a signal type meant to model a physical bus of a specific width.",vhdl;vhdl-data-types;lesson_passage,https://munsakad.github.io/Hardware-Engineering-Education-Hub/pages/course.html?slug=vhdl&lesson=vhdl-data-types,lesson:vhdl/vhdl-data-types,lesson_passage
741,Digital Logic Design,VHDL,VHDL Data Types — Constants and generics [17df338a],"constant WIDTH : integer := 8;

