end process;",vhdl;vhdl-testbenches-verification;code,https://munsakad.github.io/Hardware-Engineering-Education-Hub/pages/course.html?slug=vhdl&lesson=vhdl-testbenches-verification,lesson:vhdl/vhdl-testbenches-verification,code
807,Digital Logic Design,VHDL,Testbenches & Verification in VHDL — Self-checking with assert [c110c055],"severity error (as opposed to note or warning) is what most simulators treat as an actual test failure -- typically highlighted in the simulation log and, depending on the simulator′s settings, able to stop the run entirely.",vhdl;vhdl-testbenches-verification;lesson_passage,https://munsakad.github.io/Hardware-Engineering-Education-Hub/pages/course.html?slug=vhdl&lesson=vhdl-testbenches-verification,lesson:vhdl/vhdl-testbenches-verification,lesson_passage
