809,Digital Logic Design,VHDL,Testbenches & Verification in VHDL — Clock generation for sequential testbenches [9f885bff],"Unlike the combinational testbench above, this process deliberately has no final wait; -- it is meant to loop forever, continuously toggling clk for as long as the simulation runs, generating a free-running 10 ns-period clock exactly like the Verilog course′s always #5 clk = ~clk; pattern.",vhdl;vhdl-testbenches-verification;lesson_passage,https://munsakad.github.io/Hardware-Engineering-Education-Hub/pages/course.html?slug=vhdl&lesson=vhdl-testbenches-verification,lesson:vhdl/vhdl-testbenches-verification,lesson_passage
810,Digital Logic Design,VHDL,VHDL vs. Verilog — Two ways to describe the same hardware [82add52c],"VHDL and Verilog both describe digital hardware and both compile down to the same kinds of gates and flip-flops -- the differences are mostly about syntax style, strictness, and heritage.",vhdl;vhdl-vs-verilog;lesson_passage,https://munsakad.github.io/Hardware-Engineering-Education-Hub/pages/course.html?slug=vhdl&lesson=vhdl-vs-verilog,lesson:vhdl/vhdl-vs-verilog,lesson_passage
811,Digital Logic Design,VHDL,VHDL vs. Verilog — Two ways to describe the same hardware [066ae209],"VHDL vs. Verilog comparison | Aspect | VHDL | Verilog | Heritage | Based on Ada, originally a US DoD standard | Based on C syntax style | Typing | Strongly typed, more verbose | Weakly typed, more compact | Case sensitivity | Case-insensitive | Case-sensitive | Common industry use | Popular in defense/aerospace and some FPGA shops | Popular in commercial ASIC/FPGA design, especially US chip companies | Learning curve | More boilerplate, but catches more mistakes at compile time | Faster to write, easier to make subtle mistakes",vhdl;vhdl-vs-verilog;lesson_passage,https://munsakad.github.io/Hardware-Engineering-Education-Hub/pages/course.html?slug=vhdl&lesson=vhdl-vs-verilog,lesson:vhdl/vhdl-vs-verilog,lesson_passage
812,Digital Logic Design,VHDL,VHDL vs. Verilog — Two ways to describe the same hardware [1bd9e887],"Both languages are widely used and most FPGA/ASIC tools support both -- some teams even mix them in the same project. Learning the concepts (entities/modules, signals/wires, processes/always blocks) transfers directly between the two.",vhdl;vhdl-vs-verilog;lesson_passage,https://munsakad.github.io/Hardware-Engineering-Education-Hub/pages/course.html?slug=vhdl&lesson=vhdl-vs-verilog,lesson:vhdl/vhdl-vs-verilog,lesson_passage
813,Digital Logic Design,VHDL,VHDL vs. Verilog — Two ways to describe the same hardware [0e29f910],"Every combinational and sequential circuit built in this course -- adders, muxes, decoders, flip-flops, counters, FSMs, memory, testbenches -- has a matching implementation in the Verilog course, letting you compare both languages′ approach to the exact same problem side by side.",vhdl;vhdl-vs-verilog;lesson_passage,https://munsakad.github.io/Hardware-Engineering-Education-Hub/pages/course.html?slug=vhdl&lesson=vhdl-vs-verilog,lesson:vhdl/vhdl-vs-verilog,lesson_passage
