818,Electronics,Arduino,Arduino C++ Basics — Arduino programs are C++ [1db10e41],"An Arduino ""sketch"" is a C++ program with two required functions (setup() and loop()) and access to a large set of built-in functions for talking to pins, timers, and peripherals. Everything else about the C++ language -- variables, types, operators, control flow -- works exactly the same as it does off a microcontroller.",arduino;arduino-cpp-basics;lesson_passage,https://munsakad.github.io/Hardware-Engineering-Education-Hub/pages/course.html?slug=arduino&lesson=arduino-cpp-basics,lesson:arduino/arduino-cpp-basics,lesson_passage
819,Electronics,Arduino,Arduino C++ Basics — Variables and data types [8443206c],"A variable must be declared with a type before it is used. Common types on Arduino, and how many bytes of memory each one uses on a typical 8-bit board (like the Uno):",arduino;arduino-cpp-basics;lesson_passage,https://munsakad.github.io/Hardware-Engineering-Education-Hub/pages/course.html?slug=arduino&lesson=arduino-cpp-basics,lesson:arduino/arduino-cpp-basics,lesson_passage
820,Electronics,Arduino,Arduino C++ Basics — Variables and data types [a9feba05],"Common Arduino data types (on AVR-based boards such as the Uno) | Type | Size | Range | Typical use | bool | 1 byte | true / false | Flags, on/off states | byte | 1 byte | 0 to 255 | Raw pin values, small counters | int | 2 bytes | -32,768 to 32,767 | General-purpose whole numbers | unsigned int | 2 bytes | 0 to 65,535 | Counters that never go negative | long | 4 bytes | ≈ ±2.1 billion | Larger counters, e.g. milliseconds since startup | float | 4 bytes | ≈ ±3.4×10^38 (about 6-7 significant digits) | Sensor readings, calculations needing decimals | char | 1 byte | -128 to 127, or one character | Single characters, small numbers",arduino;arduino-cpp-basics;lesson_passage,https://munsakad.github.io/Hardware-Engineering-Education-Hub/pages/course.html?slug=arduino&lesson=arduino-cpp-basics,lesson:arduino/arduino-cpp-basics,lesson_passage
