836,Electronics,Arduino,Functions & Scope — Defining a function [bab77e0e],"A function′s return type comes first (void if it returns nothing), followed by its name and a parenthesized parameter list. setup() and loop() are simply two functions that the Arduino core calls automatically -- setup() once at startup, loop() repeatedly forever afterward.",arduino;functions-and-scope;lesson_passage,https://munsakad.github.io/Hardware-Engineering-Education-Hub/pages/course.html?slug=arduino&lesson=functions-and-scope,lesson:arduino/functions-and-scope,lesson_passage
837,Electronics,Arduino,Functions & Scope — Local vs. global variables and scope [6ebada63],"Local vs. global variables | Kind | Declared | Visible from | Lifetime | Local | Inside a function or block | Only within that function or block | Created when the block starts, destroyed when it ends | Global | Outside any function, at the top of the sketch | Every function in the file | Exists for the entire time the program runs",arduino;functions-and-scope;lesson_passage,https://munsakad.github.io/Hardware-Engineering-Education-Hub/pages/course.html?slug=arduino&lesson=functions-and-scope,lesson:arduino/functions-and-scope,lesson_passage
838,Electronics,Arduino,Functions & Scope — Local vs. global variables and scope [669af954],"Values that must survive between calls to loop() -- like a running counter, or the last time an event happened -- need to be global (or, equivalently, declared static inside the function).",arduino;functions-and-scope;lesson_passage,https://munsakad.github.io/Hardware-Engineering-Education-Hub/pages/course.html?slug=arduino&lesson=functions-and-scope,lesson:arduino/functions-and-scope,lesson_passage
