840,Electronics,Arduino,Functions & Scope — Passing parameters by value vs. by reference [b95ecd29],"By default, arguments are passed by value -- the function receives its own copy, and changes inside the function do not affect the caller′s variable. Adding & after the type makes the parameter a reference, letting the function modify the caller′s original variable directly -- useful for functions that need to report back more than one result.",arduino;functions-and-scope;lesson_passage,https://munsakad.github.io/Hardware-Engineering-Education-Hub/pages/course.html?slug=arduino&lesson=functions-and-scope,lesson:arduino/functions-and-scope,lesson_passage
