849,Electronics,Arduino,PWM & Analog Output — Duty cycle and effective voltage [38c8830f],This is the same duty-cycle idea covered for DC motor speed control in the Robotics course -- analogWrite() is simply the Arduino API for generating that PWM signal.,arduino;pwm-and-analog-output;lesson_passage,https://munsakad.github.io/Hardware-Engineering-Education-Hub/pages/course.html?slug=arduino&lesson=pwm-and-analog-output,lesson:arduino/pwm-and-analog-output,lesson_passage
850,Electronics,Arduino,PWM & Analog Output — PWM frequency [e0386fdb],"Most Arduino PWM pins switch around 490 Hz or 980 Hz by default (a few specific pins run faster) -- fast enough that an LED′s brightness or a motor′s speed appears smooth to the eye and to mechanical inertia, but potentially audible as a faint whine on some motors or speakers.",arduino;pwm-and-analog-output;lesson_passage,https://munsakad.github.io/Hardware-Engineering-Education-Hub/pages/course.html?slug=arduino&lesson=pwm-and-analog-output,lesson:arduino/pwm-and-analog-output,lesson_passage
