856,Electronics,Arduino,"Arrays, Strings & Data Structures — Arrays [a59f2101]","Arrays in C++ have a fixed size decided at compile time and are not automatically bounds-checked -- reading or writing past the end of an array silently corrupts whatever memory happens to be next to it, rather than raising an error. Always size loops using the array′s known length (or a named constant) rather than a hard-coded number that might drift out of sync.",arduino;arrays-strings-and-data-structures;lesson_passage,https://munsakad.github.io/Hardware-Engineering-Education-Hub/pages/course.html?slug=arduino&lesson=arrays-strings-and-data-structures,lesson:arduino/arrays-strings-and-data-structures,lesson_passage
