889,Electronics,Arduino,Reading Sensors — Scaling raw readings with map() [2e80eaec],"map() linearly rescales a value from one range to another -- useful anywhere a raw sensor reading needs to be converted into a more meaningful unit (degrees, percent, millivolts) before being used.",arduino;reading-sensors;lesson_passage,https://munsakad.github.io/Hardware-Engineering-Education-Hub/pages/course.html?slug=arduino&lesson=reading-sensors,lesson:arduino/reading-sensors,lesson_passage
890,Electronics,Arduino,Reading Sensors — Filtering noisy readings [69dbe532],Raw analog readings are rarely perfectly stable. A simple moving average -- averaging several consecutive readings together -- smooths out noise at the cost of reacting slightly more slowly to real changes:,arduino;reading-sensors;lesson_passage,https://munsakad.github.io/Hardware-Engineering-Education-Hub/pages/course.html?slug=arduino&lesson=reading-sensors,lesson:arduino/reading-sensors,lesson_passage
