959,Electronics,Worked calculations,Ideal ADC quantization: case 05,"An ideal 8-bit ADC with a 2.048 V reference has 2^8=256 quantization bins. Using the ideal bin-width convention, one LSB=Vref/2^N=0.008 V. This is quantization spacing, not guaranteed accuracy. Reference error, noise, input acquisition, offset and gain error can dominate; consult the converter's transfer-function convention.",worked_example;ideal_adc_quantization,https://github.com/munsakad/DMHardware-Chat-Bot/blob/main/expand_knowledge.py,calculation:Ideal ADC quantization,generated_worked_example
960,Robotics,Worked calculations,Encoder speed estimate: case 05,"An encoder produces 100 counted edges per revolution at the chosen decoding mode. If 100 edges are measured in 0.1 s, speed=edges/(edges-per-revolution×interval)=10 rev/s, or 600 RPM. Use counts per revolution after quadrature decoding, not a vendor's ambiguous PPR label, and account for any gearbox ratio.",worked_example;encoder_speed_estimate,https://github.com/munsakad/DMHardware-Chat-Bot/blob/main/expand_knowledge.py,calculation:Encoder speed estimate,generated_worked_example
961,Digital Logic Design,Worked calculations,Counter event frequency: case 05,"A 16 MHz timer clock divided by prescaler 1 drives a counter that emits an event after counting from 0 through 249 inclusive. There are TOP+1=250 ticks per event, so fevent=16000000/(1×250)=64000 Hz. A pin toggled once per event has half this square-wave frequency. Verify the timer mode, register width and clock source for actual hardware.",worked_example;counter_event_frequency,https://github.com/munsakad/DMHardware-Chat-Bot/blob/main/expand_knowledge.py,calculation:Counter event frequency,generated_worked_example
